hmmmmm...mistakes...
Everytime I make any kind of mistake, I feel immense pain. 
It hurts to realise and accept that this stupid mistakes has been
done by myself. 
Yes, I say it as "stupid mistake" because, after every mistake, I realise that "this happend because of a stupidity from my side"
It could have been avoided if I had behaved a little differently, if I had acted a little patiently.
Mostly, these mistakes happens because, my reflexes are too quick. I don't take enough time to respond. 
After every mistake from my side, I scold myself and decide that I will be more careful next time.
And Yes, The next time, I try to be more careful, but HOW MUCH MORE? May be, a very little more, just more enough to not repeat 
the same mistake again but not little more enough to not make the next mistake. So, the series of mistakes continues...

These mistakes hurts me even more, because once mistake is done, I realise, why I made this silly mistake, I could have avoided 
it easliy with being little extra cautious. May be, not even "EXTRA" cautious, just cautious. 
It's not true that I am a careless person. I don't think of myself as a careless person. 
It's not true that I am silly or, stupid. I think of myself as a sensitive person. 
I do not think that I am loser, I think, I love to win.
I also think that if I want to do something, no external force in this world can stop me.
Whatever in my life, I wanted to achieve, I achieved it by hook or, by crook.

Then, why I keep on making mistakes?
The internal force inside me wants to do everything in hurry.
The impatient person inside me is the strongest "Enemy" I have.
I want things to be done asap anyhow.
And, this "ASAP" is my enemy. I want to do things so that I can come first. 
I always want to be the winner and this nature of me, is making me a loser, making me make mistakes all the time.
